# PineNote: revert the accelerometer's mount matrix back to the device tree's value.
#
# systemd's /usr/lib/udev/hwdb.d/60-sensor.hwdb has an entry
#   sensor:modalias:of:NaccelerometerT_null_Csilan,sc7a20:*
#     ACCEL_MOUNT_MATRIX=0, 0, -1; 1, 0, 0; 0, -1, 0
# labeled as PineTab2. It matches on the **chip** (silan,sc7a20), and PineNote uses the same
# chip mounted in a different orientation — so PineTab2's calibration gets applied to this
# device, overriding the value that was already correct in the device tree
# (sysfs mount_matrix = -1, 0, 0; 0, 1, 0; 0, 0, 1).
#
# Consequence: four physical orientations collapse into two. Tested by rotating through a full
# turn — iio-sensor-proxy only ever reports normal and bottom-up, and since transform 0 and 2
# are both landscape, the screen "snaps back to landscape after turning portrait" — it never
# actually picked portrait at all.
#
# That hwdb match key (of:N<name>T<type>C<compatible>) carries no board identity, so upstream
# can't distinguish the two boards with the current format. Override directly by device
# attribute here. Numbered 61 to sort after 60-sensor's hwdb import.

SUBSYSTEM=="iio", KERNEL=="iio:device*", ATTR{name}=="sc7a20", \
  ENV{ACCEL_MOUNT_MATRIX}="-1, 0, 0; 0, 1, 0; 0, 0, 1"
